{
  "_note": "The world's pieces, drawn back to front in the order of `layers`, then in the order listed here. Positions and sizes are logical pixels of the 1440 × 900 design, which the world scales to the window. A piece with an `image` (a file path under src/world/art/) shows that image stretched to its size; without one, or when the image fails to load, the world draws a placeholder shape in its `color`, lit as `light` says. `shows` keeps a piece to some days: `open` or `closed` ones; those a change to the street from an event card is in effect, `{ \"event\": <the card's id> }`, except the changes its choices listed in an optional `except` made, such as the move away from the cones; or those a product cannot be sold, `{ \"unavailable\": <the product> }`. `text` is what a sign or a board says, in French: the road sign, the rival truck, the banner and the « Hors service » card each need one, and no other piece takes one. `fans` sets who fans themselves while it `shows`, as in a heat wave: each customer who comes then holds a fan of `color` with `chance`, which swings `swing` radians each way and back once every `periodMs` real milliseconds. `fill` makes the croissants follow the stock: `capacity` units fill the rack, shown in `steps` shelves. The `light.shadowLayer` holds no piece: the world draws the shadows on the ground there, under what stands on it.",
  "designSize": { "width": 1440, "height": 900 },
